{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c411","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1aa16-6120-7543-8e87-aff60485fd0b"},"sequence":99,"recorded_at":1780531400000193,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1aa16-642f-7fb0-a5fe-8d2aa3acfb85","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"call_id":"call_01a1aa16840574b0bdb1b89c18be9f33","command_id":"01a1aa16-642f-7fb0-a5fe-8d2aa3acfb85","correlation_facts":{"outcome":"success","tool_name":"read_file"},"kind":"tool_result","run_stream":{"id":"01a1aa16-642f-7fb0-a5fe-8d2aa3acfb85","kind":"run"},"text":"Read text file `PLAN.md`.\n(499 line(s) above)\n500|```\n501|\n502|---\n503|\n504|## 15. Tech and setup\n505|\n506|**Stack:** the my-3D2dge full engine (2D views), its `mode7`, `road`, `physics`, `rhythm` modules (all inside `my-3d2dge.js`), `Mocap` and a cut clip set, the hub client. No World3D, no other libraries. **Start from no single kit:** this game mixes genres, so use the full engine with your own page, and read `engine/kits/road.js`, `kart.js`, `rhythm.js`, `pinball.js` (physics) and `sports.js` (joining players) when you build those parts.\n507|\n508|**Fetch (✔ every command run from a clean folder; run from the dev folder):**\n509|\n510|```sh\n511|git clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git _src\n512|git -C _src sparse-checkout set dist/handoff\n513|cp -r _src/dist/handoff engine        # then remove _src\n514|npm install playwright@1.63.0         # uses the browsers already here. Never `playwright install`, whatever the engine's README says\n515|\n516|mkdir -p vendor/clipsrc/tools vendor/clipsrc/src/mocap tests/hub\n517|B=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main\n518|H=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub\n519|curl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/tools/anim-set.mjs $B/tools/anim-set.mjs\n520|curl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/tools/mocap-lib.mjs $B/tools/mocap-lib.mjs\n521|curl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/src/mocap/readable.js $B/src/mocap/readable.js    # the tool needs it exactly here\n522|curl -fsSLo vendor/readable.js $B/src/mocap/readable.js\n523|curl -fsSLo vendor/mocap.js $B/src/mocap/mocap.js\n524|for f in src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js src/mocap/sets/cmu.js examples/cmu-lib/CMU_111.js examples/cmu-lib/CMU_22.js; do curl -fsSLo vendor/clipsrc/$(basename $f) $B/$f; done\n525|curl -fsSLo vendor/session.js $H/session.js\n526|for f in harness.html bridge.js round.js; do curl -fsSLo tests/hub/$f $H/$f; done\n527|node vendor/clipsrc/tools/anim-set.mjs vendor/clipsrc/mesh2motion.js vendor/clipsrc/cmu.js vendor/clipsrc/CMU_111.js vendor/clipsrc/CMU_22.js \\\n528|  --clips \"Pushup,Meditate,Jumping Jacks,Sleeping,Victory,Cheering_Two_Hands,Dizzy,Idle_Subtle,Greeting,CMU:Run_Loop,CMU:Walk_Loop,Stretch_Yawn,Get_Up_From_Back,Waiting_Loop,Hop_One_Foot_Loop,Wave_Hello,111_38_part1,111_38_part2,111_39_part1,111_39_part2,111_39_part3,111_41_part3,22_14\" \\\n529|  --name FITCLIPS --out vendor/fitclips.js --credit \"Mesh2Motion (CC0), Quaternius (CC0), CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (free for all uses)\"\n530|# prints 23 clips, about 173 KB. vendor/clipsrc can then go; it is not bundled\n531|```\n532|\n533|More clips, if you want them: search `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/main/src/mocap/catalogs/cmu-takes.tsv` (take `NN_xx` lives in `examples/cmu-lib/CMU_NN.js`) and `.../catalogs/mesh2motion.json`.\n534|\n535|**Layout:**\n536|\n537|```\n538|engine/        the handoff copy (my-3d2dge.js is the engine; API.md, API-INDEX.md, AI_GUIDE.md, tools/, kits/, docs/)\n539|vendor/        readable.js, mocap.js, fitclips.js, session.js\n540|game/\n541|  index.html   dev page: canvas (#screen with CSS width and height 100%, or it draws at 300×150 ✔) and the scripts in order\n542|  core.js      G namespace, game, INPUT, DEV defaults, state, saves, deep links (#hub, #act/stork/1, #day/3, #ending)\n543|  balance.js   Balance model, intent sources (devices, bots), Plate\n544|  rigs.js      makeRig, setBody and moves, Tare, Gerald, joints, cast\n545|  ui.js        Pills, prompt, Card, Results, DevPanel\n546|  audio.js     songs, sfx, babble\n547|  data/        lines.js, poses.js, activities.js, charts.js, courses.js, trays.js, days.js, unlocks.js\n548|  activities/  hold.js, candle.js, rep.js, step.js, hoop.js, jog.js, slalom.js, tray.js, laundry.js\n549|  scenes/      title, attract, member, arrival, island, bodycheck, session, evening, games, ending, about, class, round\n550|tests/run.mjs  the one test command; tests/hub/ the harness\n551|build.mjs      the one build command\n552|```\n553|\n554|Plain scripts on one global `G`, no ES modules (the page must work from `file://`). **Build out by data:** a designer adds a tier, pose, chart, gate course, tray, line or day by editing `game/data/`, with no code change. Add a short `game/data/README.md` saying how.\n555|\n556|**Activity registry:**\n557|\n558|```js\n559|G.activity({ id: 'stork', family: 'hold', discipline: 'Stillness', name: 'Stork Stand', view: 'brawler', camera: { zoom: false },\n560|  class: true, hub: true, tiers: [ {/* numbers */}, {/* numbers */} ], stars: [.35, .65, .90], lines: {/* ... */},\n561|  setup(ctx) {}, update(dt, ctx) {}, draw(r, ctx) {}, hud(r, ctx) {},\n562|  result(ctx) { return { pct, detail }; },\n563|  bot(ctx, skill) { return intent; },\n564|  ghost(ctx) { return state; }, drawGhost(r, ctx, id, state) {} });\n565|```\n566|`ctx`: `{ tier, rng (seeded), contestants: [{ intent, bal, rig, name, color, score, local }], time, done, cheat }`. Every activity becomes its own pausable scene, generated from the entry. Set `game.debug = { snapshot() { return { scene, activity, tier, day, session, pct, stars, minutes, spineAge, lean, source }; } }`: tests and engine tools read it.\n567|\n568|**`build.mjs`:** concatenates engine, `vendor/readable.js`, `vendor/mocap.js`, `vendor/fitclips.js`, game files; replaces every `</script` with `<\\/script` in everything it inlines ✔; writes head tags, CSS, the boot markup at the start of `<body>` (copy the `e3-boot` div from `engine/game/index.html`); injects the exit-interview JSON as `G.ABOUT`; writes the single file to the place your brief names (pass it as an argument) and copies it to `tests/hub/game.html`. External CDN is allowed but not needed: inline everything. About 1.5 MB.\n569|\n570|**Engine changes:** only the small Dialog shadow patch (section 11) is required. Everything else works through the public API and the wrappers above. Note whatever you change, and why, for your Engine Feedback.\n571|\n572|**Traps already found (so you don't lose time on them):**\n573|1. A custom `input` map replaces the preset (section 3).\n574|2. `brawler`: +y is toward the camera (section 8).\n575|3. Mouse movement doesn't change `lastDevice` from `'keyboard'` (section 3).\n576|4. Default `music` is .5 and `glyphs` 'auto': set both (section 11).\n577|5. Music at 10% hides the beat: click on the sfx bus (section 4).\n578|6. HTML menus lack hover focus; the touch notice is 88% opaque (section 11).\n579|7. `E.Dialog` hard-codes a dark text shadow (section 11). The standard Settings list is long at 10 feet: rely on its scrolling focus and the zoom CSS.\n580|8. In tests, `game.fadeTime = 0`; `game.go` otherwise delays the new scene .22 s.\n581|9. A frame past 50 ms gives up its time: browser tests here are software-rendered and slow, so wait on game state, never on the clock.\n582|10. In Python Playwright use `page.wait_for_timeout`, not `time.sleep` (it freezes the event loop and frames never appear).\n583|11. `E.store` is shared by id; set `id` on the game, and `E.store.clear()` between test games in one process.\n584|12. Fixed-camera scenes need `camera: { zoom: false }`, or the wheel zooms instead of stepping.\n585|\n586|---\n587|\n588|## 16. Testing\n589|\n590|**One command: `node tests/run.mjs [rules|browser|hub|all]`.** It prints only failures and one final line (`213 passed, 0 failed`). Rerun only the group whose code you changed. Use scripted checks first and screenshots only for what a script can't judge. Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n591|\n592|**`rules` (Node, no browser, seconds).** Load engine, vendor and game files in a `vm` context with `window`, `addEventListener` and `location` stand-ins (✔ `Mocap` and clips load this way; see `engine/kits/test.mjs`). Drive with `game.advance` and `input.tap/hold`; read `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n593|- Lean model: each row of the section 3 table lands in its band (±10 points) with the bots, on 12 seeds.\n594|- Every activity, every tier: passive under 1★; average at least 1★; good at least 2★; finishes in its time; `game.errors` stays empty.\n595|- **Full scripted playthrough:** New Member through every scene to the Ending using real input taps and bots, all 12 activities played, Spine Age falls, Day 3 plateau holds, unlocks arrive, Free Play opens. Also a passive run (the worst player still reaches the end).\n596|- Saves: reload gives the same state; 3 members stay separate; a damaged save doesn't crash.\n597|- Same seed and same input give the same hash twice.\n598|- Attract: fires at 10 s idle (and not at 9.9), visits every playlist item, any input returns to title, no save or unlock changed.\n599|- Dev: every slider changes its live value; reset restores all; every jump target loads.\n600|- Class: 4 inputs, scores, podium. Hub logic with a fake `AIHub` object: same seed, same deal; time-up reports once; end stops input.\n601|- Data lint: every line, pose, clip name, activity and unlock referenced exists; no `TODO` or placeholder strings in `game/`.\n602|\n603|**`browser` (Playwright, one browser at a time, on the built file via `file://`, which needs no server):**\n604|- `node engine/tools/check.mjs <built file>` passes with no errors (and act on its look notes), at 1280×720.\n605|- **Controller stand-in ✔:** `add_init_script` replaces `navigator.getGamepads` with a `'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD)'` pad in `mapping: 'standard'`. Check axes lean, `buttons[7].value` reads through `input.value`, ✕ confirms, prompts show ✕, Settings to Xbox shows A.\n606|- Keyboard and mouse: WASD nudges; pointer leans; hover moves focus in `Pills` and in the HTML menus; click activates; prompts change with the device.\n607|- Touch-only: a phone profile shows the notice and Settings button, no touch controls, and attract starts at 10 s behind it. iPhone profile on WebKit as a smoke test; also load in Firefox.\n608|- Sound: after a gesture, an `AnalyserNode` on the music bus is non-silent and `game.settings.music === .1` on fresh storage; the voice bus sounds during dialog; `OfflineAudioContext` renders `babble` non-silent; no audio files and no network requests at all (`page.on('request')`).\n609|- 1920×1080 screenshots for the 10-foot judgement of title, Plate, Card, results and island: look at them once per milestone.\n610|\n611|**`hub`:** copy the bundle to `tests/hub/game.html`, serve `tests/hub` with `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, read the port it prints, confirm the page is yours, then open `harness.html?game=game.html&` + each of: `players=1&auto=1`; `players=2&auto=1`; `players=3&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave`. Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, require `window.__hubCheck.pass`, and print failing `checks`. Then open the game on its own and see it reach the title. Stop only your server, by its PID, never with `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`.\n612|\n613|**Sharing this computer:** keep one or two browsers open, keep every file in your own folder, don't read the folders beside it (other agents work there), never kill anything you did not start. \"Target closed\" or \"page crashed\" means memory ran out: run fewer browsers rather than retrying.\n614|\n615|---\n616|\n617|## 17. Build order\n618|\n619|Each milestone ends with a playable game and green tests. Keep the build and the tests working from M0 onward.\n620|\n621|| # | Build | Done when |\n622||---|---|---|\n623|| M0 | Fetch; `build.mjs`; `tests/run.mjs`; `INPUT`, Shell theme, settings; empty title and round scenes with the session wrapper | Harness passes on the empty game; music .1; `tests/run.mjs` prints its line |\n624|| M1 | Lean, intent, devices, bots, Plate; `makeRig`; Tare and voice; studio scene; **Stork Stand** with Card and Results | Feels good on stick, keys and mouse. Bands hold. **Stop and tune here: it is the whole game** |\n625|| M2 | Title, Pills, Member Card, Arrival, island, mats, Body Check, Day loop, evening, saves, Gerald, Spine Age; attract skeleton; Dev panel with Lean sliders | A day can be lived start to end |\n626|| M3 | Sun Flow, Quiet Candle, all three Rail exercises | Bots pass; poses read at 1080p |\n627|| M4 | Step Class, Hoop Hips, Coastal Jog | Bots pass; beat audible at default volume |\n628|| M5 | Slalom, Tray Service, Laundry Line | Bots pass |\n629|| M6 | Five-day script, Tare's Day, Gentle Games, duel, Ending, Credits, Free Play, wardrobe, full line bank, all music and sfx | Full playthrough test passes |\n630|| M7 | Class mode; the hub round with ghosts and card | Harness at all five settings; two-page play shows ghosts |\n631|| M8 | Full attract, full Dev Mode with Pose Viewer, About screen, tier 2s, Comfort, polish pass (particles, stamps, rumble, transitions: `game.go` with `fade: 'iris'`) | All groups green |\n632|| M9 | Final bundle, exit interview parses, About matches it, brief checklist below | Done |\n633|\n634|**If you truly run out of room, cut in this order and remove every trace (no stubs):** tier 2s except Eyes Closed → Tare's Day scene → Laundry Line → Coastal Jog → wardrobe items beyond three. Never cut: the Lean, Stork, Rail, Step, Candle, Slalom, Tray, the day loop, the ending, attract, dev mode, Class, the hub round, About.\n635|\n636|---\n637|\n638|## 18. Finish line: your brief, line by line\n639|\n640|- [ ] Title chosen by the brief's method and shown on the title screen; single HTML file with the brief's name in the brief's place; dev files in the brief's dev folder\n641|- [ ] Original game: no copied names, characters, art, music or levels\n642|- [ ] Genre and perspective as section 1; built on the handoff engine (changes noted)\n643|- [ ] Art and animation: engine-native base, new assets and motion (sections 8, 9)\n644|- [ ] All audio from code; gibberish voices; music 10% by default (section 10)\n645|- [ ] Hub session passes the harness; the game also runs on its own, with local Class (section 14)\n646|- [ ] Demo shows every feature; all infrastructure is real; designer data in `game/data/` (section 15)\n647|- [ ] Dev Mode from the pause menu: tools, live sliders, reset (section 13)\n648|- [ ] Attract at 10 s idle, loops, any input exits, runs on touch-only (section 12)\n649|- [ ] Writing in the source-inspired tone throughout (section 7)\n650|- [ ] 10-foot, controller-first; native keyboard and mouse; hover moves focus; prompts follow last device; PlayStation glyphs with Xbox setting; no dense screens (section 11)\n651|- [ ] Touch-only: no touch controls, \"Controller or keyboard required\", Settings button (section 11)\n652|- [ ] One test command, failures and a count only; scripted playthrough of the whole game (section 16)\n653|- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders or stubs anywhere\n654|- [ ] Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback in the chat reply **and** the About screen, \"unknown\" for what you can't confirm, Usage as \"added on import\". Plan field: this plan's file name. Research field: what you actually did (further research is optional; this plan's recipes are already tested)\n655|- [ ] Exit-interview JSON beside the HTML, in the brief's exact shape, parses. Suggested `aiHub`: type `Game`, genre `Sports`, source `Wii Fit`, series empty, players `1–4`, controls in one line, tags from: `pixel art`, `comedy`, `versus`, `arcade`, `story`, `2d`"}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c413","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1aa16-6120-7543-8e87-aff60485fd0b"},"sequence":100,"recorded_at":1780531400000195,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1aa16-642f-7fb0-a5fe-8d2aa3acfb85","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"call_id":"call_01a1aa16849a70738ec18b03f2b8bf43","command_id":"01a1aa16-642f-7fb0-a5fe-8d2aa3acfb85","correlation_facts":{"outcome":"success","tool_name":"bash"},"kind":"tool_result","run_stream":{"id":"01a1aa16-642f-7fb0-a5fe-8d2aa3acfb85","kind":"run"},"text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-1-1\",\n  \"command\": \"ls -la; echo \\\"---\\\"; ls -la .agents 2>/dev/null; cat *.md 2>/dev/null | head -n 20; echo \\\"---workspace files---\\\"; find . -maxdepth 2 -type f | head -n 100\",\n  \"description\": \"List workspace contents\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"total 92\\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  4 22:02 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 micha micha  4096 Nov  4 22:02 ..\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 65097 Nov  4 22:02 PLAN.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   219 Nov  4 22:02 STAGE.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 12511 Nov  4 22:02 TASK.md\\n---\\n# Build plan: a wellness-retreat balance game inspired by Wii Fit\\n\\nYou are building this game alone, from this plan and your brief. Nobody can answer questions, so decide and move on.\\n\\n- **Your brief wins** on anything it states: deliverable names, the title rule, what the About screen lists, the exit interview. Where it leaves a choice, this plan has made it.\\n- **The title is yours.** Pick it the way your brief says. This plan says \\\"the title\\\" wherever it appears.\\n- **Paths here are relative to your dev folder.** The final file's name and place are in your brief.\\n- **✔ means tested.** It was run on this computer against engine v0.88.0 and hub client 1.4.0 while this plan was written. Trust those recipes. Numbers marked \\\"start\\\" are tuning defaults: change them with the dev sliders.\\n- Read sections 1 to 4 and 15 to 17 first. Use the rest as reference while you build each part.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. The game\\n\\n**In one line:** a gentle, deadpan comedy about a five-day stay at a wellness retreat, where one analog skill, your balance, drives twelve short sports and exercise activities, coached by a needy talking scale and two serene wooden instructors.\\n\\n- **Genre:** sports and fitness minigame collection inside a light life-sim routine. Catalogue genre: Sports.\\n- **Perspective:** chosen per activity, always the clearest view of the body:\\n\\n| Where | View | Why |\\n---workspace files---\\n./PLAN.md\\n./STAGE.md\\n./TASK.md\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 1687,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 422,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}"}}
