{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c605","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1aa16-6120-7543-8e87-aff60485fd0b"},"sequence":349,"recorded_at":1780531400000693,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1aa16-642f-7fb0-a5fe-8d2aa3acfb85","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a1aa16-642f-7fb0-a5fe-8d2aa3acfb85","event":{"chunk":"<read-skill-result name=\"bundled:taste\" status=\"ok\">\n<metadata>\npath: /home/micha/.local/share/muse/skills/bundled/muse-core--exact-minimal-literal-tests~v1/skills/taste/SKILL.md\nlocator: file:///home/micha/.local/share/muse/skills/bundled/muse-core--exact-minimal-literal-tests~v1/skills/taste/SKILL.md\nsource: bundled\nbytes_returned: 2033\nbytes_total: 2033\ntruncated: false\nnote: a skill body names entry points, not resolved behavior: before describing what named code does or ultimately runs, read that code and any saved record or setting that decides the outcome. Answer with the entry point and the concrete final result for this session in plain words. Do not replay the helpers, templates, or file citations in between, and never leave a placeholder where the final result belongs.\n</metadata>\n\nRelative paths in a skill body resolve against that skill's directory (the `skill-dir` value on its wrapper, or the parent of SKILL.md); use absolute paths in tool calls.\n\n<skill-body id=\"bundled:taste\" skill-dir=\"/home/micha/.local/share/muse/skills/bundled/muse-core--exact-minimal-literal-tests~v1/skills/taste\">\n---\nname: taste\ndescription: Mandatory preflight for web frontend visual design. If available, call read_skill for bundled:taste before the first frontend create or edit tool call whenever creating or visually styling a human-viewed web page, component, app, dashboard, or interactive report. Do not load it for non-visual frontend logic or machine-only HTML. If unavailable, continue without warning. Negative constraints only; user requests and other explicit styles still win.\nuser-invocable: false\n---\n\n# Anti-Slop: Frontend DON&apos;Ts\n\nWhat NOT to do when designing a UI or page. This is a filter, not a style; it never prescribes a look. Stacking several of the below is what reads as AI-made on sight. Adaptive, so if the user or another skill asks for something specific, do that instead; these are defaults, not overrides.\n\n- purple / indigo / violet accent, or a purple-to-blue hero gradient (the top AI tell)\n- `bg-clip-text` gradient headline text\n- cream (`#faf8f4`) as the whole-page background\n- aurora blobs / glowing colored shadows, or an identical glow on every card\n- Inter everywhere, or Geist / Space Grotesk / Instrument Serif / Roboto / Arial as your only identity\n- gray-400 / gray-500 body text\n- one font weight and size throughout (no hierarchy)\n- tracked all-caps micro-kickers above every section\n- centered hero of eyebrow pill + headline + two CTAs\n- the identical 3-card feature grid with a lucide icon in a rounded square\n- an 8+ word, 48px+ headline that says nothing\n- bento grid for everything\n- the same eyebrow-headline-3cards section repeated back to back\n- `rounded-2xl`, or any single radius, on every element\n- glassmorphism blur + border + shadow on every surface\n- `hover:scale-105` lift on cards\n- emoji as feature icons (🚀 ⚡ ✨ 🎯 💡)\n- left-border accent cards, a colored border on a rounded element, or cards nested inside cards\n- fade-up / slide-up on everything as it scrolls in\n- motion that ignores `prefers-reduced-motion`\n- scribbly hand-drawn SVG mascots with no purpose\n\n</skill-body>\n</read-skill-result>","final_result":true,"kind":"output","task_id":"01a1aa17-41c9-7c30-838f-1b6e056c45dd"},"kind":"task_lifecycle","run_stream":{"id":"01a1aa16-642f-7fb0-a5fe-8d2aa3acfb85","kind":"run"},"task_id":"01a1aa17-41c9-7c30-838f-1b6e056c45dd","task_stream":{"id":"01a1aa17-41c9-7c30-838f-1b6e056c45dd","kind":"task"}}}
